WEBVTT

00:01.420 --> 00:04.630
<b>KEIO YEAR 3 (1867)</b>

02:30.960 --> 02:32.540
Well, what's your next move?

02:57.420 --> 02:58.750
Just a tad too slow.

02:58.750 --> 03:00.790
I-I... surrender.

03:02.750 --> 03:06.830
Candor is among your best qualities,
but it can also be a pitfall.

03:08.130 --> 03:09.380
How humiliating.

03:09.540 --> 03:11.830
You're as tough as ever, Jin-dono.

03:12.330 --> 03:15.750
I have nothing but respect
for your refined swordsmanship.

03:17.040 --> 03:21.960
I'm ashamed to say I haven't had much chance
to wield my blade on a actual battlefield.

03:22.380 --> 03:25.670
Great work, honey.
You and Jinya-sama both fought hard.

03:29.170 --> 03:31.040
Kinu. Sorry to trouble you.

03:36.500 --> 03:37.830
Be careful now.

03:40.500 --> 03:41.330
Thank you.

03:47.040 --> 03:49.080
Much obliged, Kinu-dono.

03:49.080 --> 03:52.580
Think nothing of it. This is the least I can do
for you indulging my husband.

03:52.790 --> 03:55.920
I don't mind. It proved beneficial for me as well.

03:56.290 --> 03:58.830
Well, I'm most glad to hear that.

03:59.330 --> 04:00.500
By the way...

04:00.880 --> 04:01.540
Yes?

04:01.960 --> 04:06.500
Is it okay if I just drop all the genteel speak now, ronin?

04:09.420 --> 04:11.500
I would prefer that, honestly.

04:11.790 --> 04:13.830
It's fine to call me "Harlot," you know.

04:14.250 --> 04:16.580
I can't refer to a married woman like a tramp.

04:16.960 --> 04:18.420
Such a stiff.

04:18.420 --> 04:23.170
That's funny, considering you didn't seem
to notice we got married until we told you about it.

04:23.170 --> 04:24.670
When will you let me live that down?

04:24.670 --> 04:26.500
Jinya-sama! Nomari-san!

04:26.500 --> 04:29.000
Oh, Tadanobu! Welcome home.

04:29.130 --> 04:30.330
Here to spar?

04:30.330 --> 04:32.960
Yes. We just finished a bout.

04:33.170 --> 04:35.330
Aww, I wish I could've seen it.

04:37.580 --> 04:40.330
Greetings, Nomari-san. Serendipity is a beautiful thing.

04:40.670 --> 04:43.170
Huh? Serendippy is bootyful?

04:46.460 --> 04:49.040
Tadanobu seems to have taken quite a liking to Nomari.

04:49.920 --> 04:51.130
What do you think, Jin-dono?

04:51.830 --> 04:54.710
Would you ever let your daughter
marry into a samurai family?

04:56.460 --> 04:58.040
You can't have her.

04:58.460 --> 05:00.290
First, you wrap a string around this part here.

04:58.460 --> 04:59.880
Or so I'd like to say.

04:59.880 --> 05:02.830
But I suppose that might give me more peace of mind

05:00.290 --> 05:00.920
Uh-huh.

05:00.920 --> 05:02.830
Then you pull it to make it spin.

05:02.830 --> 05:04.670
than her marrying a total stranger.

05:03.290 --> 05:04.670
Do you want to try it with me?

05:05.000 --> 05:05.670
Yeah!

05:05.960 --> 05:07.420
All right. Here we go!

05:06.330 --> 05:08.330
But it all depends on Nomari.

05:09.170 --> 05:12.460
I want her to decide when she gets older.

05:13.380 --> 05:14.460
What's so funny?

05:14.460 --> 05:18.710
Nothing. It just feels strange
that we're both fussing over our kids.

05:19.210 --> 05:21.920
Makes me realize how old we've gotten.

05:22.290 --> 05:24.920
This would've been unthinkable
back in the early days, huh?

05:26.750 --> 05:27.960
I must say, Jin-dono...

05:29.000 --> 05:30.170
...you haven't changed.

05:34.170 --> 05:37.130
Oh! My apologies. Forget I said anything.

05:37.170 --> 05:39.630
Well, it's about time that we get going.

05:40.170 --> 05:41.460
Nomari! Get ready to go.

05:42.170 --> 05:43.170
Please wait!

05:43.500 --> 05:45.170
I didn't mean to offend you!

05:45.170 --> 05:46.540
You haven't.

05:46.880 --> 05:49.000
I just want to swing by the soba shop.

05:50.080 --> 05:51.170
I see.

05:55.630 --> 05:57.630
Oh? Heading home already?

05:58.380 --> 05:59.000
Yeah.

05:59.000 --> 06:02.790
Your face looks glum.
Was it something my husband said?

06:03.710 --> 06:04.580
Not really.

06:04.830 --> 06:05.710
All right, then.

06:06.210 --> 06:08.580
Drop by again sometime, okay?

06:09.250 --> 06:10.330
What's wrong?

06:11.580 --> 06:12.380
I'm surprised.

06:12.960 --> 06:15.380
I didn't think that I'd be welcome here.

06:15.920 --> 06:17.960
Don't be ridiculous.

06:17.960 --> 06:21.250
Although I'm sure you must feel
rather uncomfortable around me.

06:21.880 --> 06:24.170
You're always so easy to read!

06:26.670 --> 06:28.290
Here's a piece of advice.

06:28.460 --> 06:31.040
Try not to be so hard on yourself.

06:31.710 --> 06:35.330
Life is a gift, but it's always a mix of good and bad.

06:35.330 --> 06:37.460
Change also comes in the same flavors.

06:38.420 --> 06:43.170
I don't know what kind of albatross is around your neck,
but you wouldn't be the same without it, right?

06:43.830 --> 06:46.830
I actually prefer you more than most, ronin.

06:47.790 --> 06:49.460
And I'm sure he feels the same.

06:51.380 --> 06:54.210
Never imagined I'd be getting a peptalk from you.

06:54.830 --> 06:56.500
Jeez, cold much?

06:56.920 --> 06:59.790
But hey, that's just true to form for us.

07:09.170 --> 07:12.080
Oh, Jinya-kun. And Nomari-chan.

07:12.670 --> 07:13.580
Where's your dad?

07:15.290 --> 07:16.670
Resting in the back.

07:18.080 --> 07:20.750
I see. He does that a lot these days.

07:22.580 --> 07:24.750
It's all my fault.

07:28.500 --> 07:30.210
No words of comfort, huh?

07:30.790 --> 07:32.330
Would you prefer I say something?

07:32.790 --> 07:33.580
No.

07:34.080 --> 07:37.830
Because even if you did,
I wouldn't be able to take it to heart.

07:43.290 --> 07:46.380
We never saw Grampy! He slept all day, huh?

07:48.750 --> 07:49.750
Yeah...

07:54.380 --> 07:55.630
Welcome in, pal!

07:56.540 --> 07:58.500
Ah! It's Grampy!

07:58.790 --> 08:00.580
Hi there, sweet pea.

08:01.210 --> 08:03.080
Are you doing all right?

08:03.080 --> 08:06.130
Y'know, I'm actually full of beans today!

08:06.130 --> 08:08.790
So I figured I'd whip up some soba for once.

08:08.790 --> 08:12.080
Dad. Just promise me you won't push yourself.

08:13.250 --> 08:14.460
Here. Order up.

08:14.630 --> 08:15.460
Thank you.

08:15.630 --> 08:16.960
C'mon, you too, Ofuu!

08:17.460 --> 08:19.500
Huh? But...

08:19.500 --> 08:21.290
Aw, don't fuss. Gotta treat yourself sometimes.

08:21.790 --> 08:24.710
He's right. This is a rare opportunity.

08:28.420 --> 08:32.170
Thinking about it, we go back a long time, eh, pal?

08:32.630 --> 08:34.540
More than a decade now.

08:35.710 --> 08:39.580
You were sitting here eating
kake-soba back when we first met, too.

08:40.040 --> 08:42.630
Looking exactly the same as you do now.

08:43.250 --> 08:45.380
Though, you didn't have a daughter then.

08:56.580 --> 09:01.630
Boy! Living to old age was worth it
just to see that dopey grin on your face, pal!

09:02.080 --> 09:05.880
Give me a break. I already know how silly I must look.

09:05.880 --> 09:07.960
Heavens no! It's a perfect fit for ya!

09:08.880 --> 09:11.710
Ya look far better as a dad than a demon hunter.

09:13.500 --> 09:19.420
Think about her future. It's about time ya stopped
risking your skin out there hunting demons, no?

09:19.920 --> 09:23.920
If it's money you're worried about,
then just work here instead.

09:24.790 --> 09:30.330
Imagine it. You can get hitched with my Ofuu
and take over the soba shop!

09:31.630 --> 09:34.130
Sorry. I don't think that's possible.

09:34.670 --> 09:37.170
"Demons cannot defy their nature as demons."

09:38.460 --> 09:40.330
One of them told me as much.

09:40.790 --> 09:45.000
Demons live under the spell of their emotions
and perish in the name of their purpose.

09:45.540 --> 09:47.080
I've always believed that.

09:47.540 --> 09:54.040
No matter how much time passes, I will remain
unchanged and driven by the feelings in my heart

09:54.710 --> 09:57.380
until I eventually breath my last.

09:57.380 --> 10:00.130
Well, you've definitely changed in the time I've known ya.

10:00.580 --> 10:01.750
Only a little.

10:02.330 --> 10:05.500
But not in essence. I simply learned how to take a detour.

10:06.000 --> 10:10.040
When the time ultimately comes,
I'll still cast everything aside.

10:11.000 --> 10:13.330
And that keeps you from living a normal life?

10:14.000 --> 10:16.040
Come on. You're really gonna accept that?

10:16.250 --> 10:19.960
It's never bothered me. Because I had a goal to fulfill.

10:21.170 --> 10:26.710
But for reasons I'm unsure of...
right now, that way of life feels a little encumbering.

10:29.960 --> 10:31.790
Then why not just forsake all of it?

10:32.130 --> 10:34.630
If I could do that, I'd never have turned demon.

10:36.750 --> 10:40.670
Well, it's a good thing. At least if you ask me.

10:41.330 --> 10:44.500
The fact you feel encumbered by that way of life
just goes to show how much

10:44.500 --> 10:47.540
you're enjoying what you have now.

10:48.170 --> 10:50.630
So the idea of casting it aside makes you lonely.

10:51.130 --> 10:53.130
This shop, and all of us in it,

10:53.460 --> 10:58.460
have become equally as precious to you
as the purpose you're so bent on fulfilling, get it?

10:59.080 --> 11:01.080
Ain't nothing more joyous than that!

11:01.920 --> 11:05.000
I see. It was loneliness I felt, huh?

11:06.630 --> 11:09.790
I'm as spineless as ever, I suppose.

11:11.040 --> 11:11.830
Ofuu.

11:12.250 --> 11:13.750
Will you two hear me out?

11:17.670 --> 11:23.580
You're both gonna live a heck of a lot longer
and lose far more than I ever will.

11:24.250 --> 11:26.630
Naturally, the things you lose will never come back.

11:27.250 --> 11:28.960
Though, it's kinda strange...

11:29.500 --> 11:33.040
because those things always seem
more beautiful in our mind's eye.

11:33.580 --> 11:36.670
But listen, there ain't nothing wrong with that.

11:37.080 --> 11:39.830
When the old times pop into your head
and make you wanna cry,

11:40.040 --> 11:41.420
be proud of it!

11:41.880 --> 11:48.040
Because it's proof that you've built something
for yourself that's worth getting sad over.

11:48.920 --> 11:49.880
But do me a favor.

11:50.500 --> 11:55.170
Please don't let the fear of saying goodbye
make you neglect the present.

11:56.080 --> 11:59.420
There'll always be times when remembering the past
makes you want to hate everything.

11:59.960 --> 12:05.330
But you two are special, you can go beyond that
to find happiness with other people.

12:05.790 --> 12:10.460
Your long lifespans are precisely what make
living in the present such an important experience.

12:11.580 --> 12:14.630
That's what I believe is best for you.

12:16.710 --> 12:21.130
Whew! Now did that make me sound like
a proper dad or what?

12:21.380 --> 12:24.500
It's not even a question. You're Ofuu's father, aren't you?

12:24.920 --> 12:27.880
You just got a different start from most people.

12:27.920 --> 12:31.500
Yes. I've never been more proud to have you as my dad.

12:31.830 --> 12:34.170
Hey. I got a little request of you three.

12:34.460 --> 12:36.330
Couldja all stand up over there?

12:36.630 --> 12:37.580
What for?

12:37.580 --> 12:38.920
C'mon. Please?

12:40.040 --> 12:42.880
Go stand next to him Ofuu. There ya go.

12:43.130 --> 12:44.580
That's perfect.

12:45.170 --> 12:49.830
And now, sweet pea.
Couldja grab hold of both their hands?

13:10.130 --> 13:15.210
Wow. Now that's truly a sight to behold.

13:17.750 --> 13:21.670
Whew! I pooped myself out doing all this work today!

13:22.080 --> 13:24.380
Ofuu. Clean up the shop for me, would ya?

13:25.040 --> 13:27.380
Well, see y'all tomorrow.

13:32.330 --> 13:34.250
After retiring to his bedroom,

13:34.670 --> 13:37.500
Sadanaga Hyoma Miura went to sleep...

13:38.080 --> 13:39.250
and never woke up again.

14:06.250 --> 14:08.040
It's never felt so spacious before.

14:08.880 --> 14:12.420
I knew this would happen. Our lifespans are different.

14:12.790 --> 14:14.630
We couldn't be together forever.

14:15.420 --> 14:19.880
That's why I tried to push Hyoma away...

14:20.290 --> 14:22.580
to drive him out of my garden of happiness.

14:23.500 --> 14:27.170
But his kindness got the better of me,

14:27.670 --> 14:30.210
now I'm devastated over what I knew was coming.

14:30.920 --> 14:32.040
It's pathetic, isn't it?

14:32.500 --> 14:34.380
I haven't changed in the slightest.

14:36.750 --> 14:37.880
Jinya-kun...

14:39.330 --> 14:42.080
Please let me stay like this for a little while.

14:43.710 --> 14:46.960
I can never remember a time when your dad
wasn't worried about you.

14:47.790 --> 14:51.170
I swear, despite how much he joked
about me doting on Nomari,

14:51.750 --> 14:54.040
that man was the undisputed king of doting fathers.

14:54.920 --> 14:55.500
Yes.

14:56.580 --> 15:00.210
He honestly never thought about anything but me.

15:00.920 --> 15:06.290
This is just the beginning, isn't it?
We're going to suffer losses like this over and over.

15:10.130 --> 15:12.380
Such a long road ahead...

15:13.750 --> 15:16.330
Yes. Very long.

15:26.420 --> 15:27.420
I'm sorry.

15:27.420 --> 15:28.040
It's okay.

15:30.630 --> 15:32.250
Thank you so much.

15:32.250 --> 15:33.670
But I didn't do anything.

15:34.330 --> 15:38.250
You stayed with me, didn't you?
That was a huge comfort.

15:39.710 --> 15:40.210
Pardon.

15:40.210 --> 15:42.080
Daddy! We're back!

15:42.080 --> 15:43.630
Sorry to make you watch her.

15:43.790 --> 15:44.830
I don't mind.

15:45.750 --> 15:47.420
Did you have a good time, Nomari?

15:48.170 --> 15:48.790
Uh-huh!

15:50.000 --> 15:52.670
Jin-dono. I need to speak with you.

15:54.540 --> 15:56.380
All right. Let's go someplace else.

15:56.540 --> 16:00.000
No. Here is fine, since I'd like Ofuu-san to hear this, too.

16:00.210 --> 16:01.630
Me, really?

16:01.750 --> 16:05.540
Yes. This shop always held a special place
in my heart, after all.

16:09.170 --> 16:10.540
I'm going to Kyoto.

16:11.580 --> 16:14.750
I'm leaving Edo behind and dedicating myself
to overthrowing the shogunate.

16:15.250 --> 16:16.130
Are you sure?

16:16.960 --> 16:18.960
The government has already collapsed.

16:19.330 --> 16:24.040
Despite all the citizens who are in need of help,
our leaders still do nothing but bow to foreign powers.

16:24.920 --> 16:28.460
As a samurai, I swore my loyalty to Tokugawa,

16:28.920 --> 16:32.330
but the bushido code compels me
to protect the powerless.

16:33.040 --> 16:38.500
I cannot just sit here and pretend everything is okay,
while people continue to suffer day in and day out.

16:40.130 --> 16:41.250
I'm going to fight.

16:41.710 --> 16:44.670
And hopefully, usher this country into a new era.

16:45.170 --> 16:46.630
So we can see a brighter future.

16:46.960 --> 16:49.460
Even if it comes at the cost of your life?

16:50.210 --> 16:54.000
I'll embrace death with open arms if that's
what it takes to forge a path to the future.

16:54.790 --> 16:56.710
But what about Kinu-san?

16:57.290 --> 16:58.630
We've already talked it over.

16:59.330 --> 17:00.710
She's going to Kyoto with me.

17:01.670 --> 17:03.130
She has samurai blood in her.

17:04.540 --> 17:05.920
And is headstrong to boot.

17:07.380 --> 17:08.830
I see...

17:08.830 --> 17:09.920
Then you should go.

17:10.540 --> 17:12.830
Follow the path in life that you've settled on.

17:13.210 --> 17:17.580
Right. Frankly, I'm not sure how useful
I can actually be on the battlefield.

17:18.080 --> 17:20.040
But even so, I am a samurai.

17:20.210 --> 17:24.630
I owe it to my ancestors to act in defense
of the people until the bitter end.

17:30.290 --> 17:32.580
Good grief. You can be a real pain in the neck.

17:32.790 --> 17:34.880
You're the last person I want to hear that from, Jin-dono.

17:38.380 --> 17:41.170
Cheers to your new journey. Drinks are on me.

17:43.920 --> 17:46.330
When will you be leaving?

17:46.330 --> 17:49.750
Tomorrow. I figured the earlier the better.

17:50.210 --> 17:53.830
Then you better drink light, so you don't get a hangover.

17:54.380 --> 17:58.000
Actually, I was going to pass on any drinks,
seeing as it's the middle of the day...

17:59.170 --> 18:03.250
You have Nomari-chan to look after, Jinya-kun.
Don't drink too much yourself.

18:03.250 --> 18:04.080
Fair enough.

18:04.630 --> 18:09.460
I'm dead set on going to Kyoto, but I must admit
that I'll regret never getting to see this scenery again.

18:09.580 --> 18:12.170
Oh, please. Don't put it like that!

18:12.170 --> 18:15.210
What she said. You're not going to the grave just yet.

18:15.210 --> 18:17.500
Oh? Going to Kyoto, are we?

18:18.170 --> 18:19.830
That's quite interesting.

18:20.420 --> 18:23.130
Seems you're all over the place, as usual.

18:23.500 --> 18:26.420
Finally gotten fed up with me, have you?

18:26.670 --> 18:28.920
I'm actually here for the samurai.

18:28.920 --> 18:30.420
You mean me?

18:30.830 --> 18:36.040
My master has connections within the shogunate.
They've been sharing some concerning rumors.

18:36.750 --> 18:39.790
Mostly regarding a certain
samurai stealing official documents.

18:39.790 --> 18:41.710
The thief could only be an administrative clerk.

18:41.710 --> 18:45.460
And my master believes that any signs of treachery
must not be overlooked.

18:45.460 --> 18:46.710
I've done no such thing!

18:46.710 --> 18:50.710
Let's just cut to the chase.
Your master has ordered you to kill Naotsugu, yes?

18:52.380 --> 18:57.380
My duty is simple. To eliminate anything
and anyone who stands in my master's way!

19:08.790 --> 19:11.580
Thus, you will die here.

19:14.330 --> 19:15.750
My God! Look!

19:17.130 --> 19:18.710
It's some kind of monster!

19:31.630 --> 19:33.250
Your attacks are sharp and swift.

19:33.670 --> 19:36.170
It makes sense you're able to fell
demons with just one blade.

19:36.500 --> 19:37.580
Take Nomari and go.

19:37.580 --> 19:38.290
Okay!

19:38.630 --> 19:40.500
Naotsugu. You should get out of here, too.

19:40.500 --> 19:43.500
But, Jin-dono! I'm the one it wants!

19:44.420 --> 19:45.670
I hunt demons.

19:45.960 --> 19:47.880
That's my calling in life.

19:52.290 --> 19:54.080
And so, it comes down to us.

19:54.330 --> 19:56.580
I imagine you won't back down no matter what I say.

19:56.790 --> 19:57.630
Obviously.

20:17.790 --> 20:18.710
That won't work!

20:24.540 --> 20:30.130
Unfortunately for you, there is no blade sharp enough
to cut through me.

20:30.630 --> 20:32.880
For my body is indomitable.

20:38.420 --> 20:39.380
Oh?

20:42.080 --> 20:43.960
This man is my friend.

20:44.460 --> 20:45.670
I won't let you kill him!

20:46.080 --> 20:49.880
Hilarious. You think you stand any chance against me?

20:49.880 --> 20:52.750
There comes a time when
every samurai must stand their ground!

20:57.080 --> 20:59.000
Very well, Naotsugu Miura.

20:59.250 --> 21:02.460
As per my master's orders, you shall meet your end here!

21:02.790 --> 21:05.080
Naotsugu! Stop!

21:05.540 --> 21:06.290
You can't win...

21:06.290 --> 21:08.790
You heard me! I'm not leaving!

21:14.880 --> 21:16.000
You're dead.

21:18.920 --> 21:21.250
Not again. Can't I protect anything?!

21:40.500 --> 21:41.580
Brawn.

21:58.290 --> 21:59.250
Steadfast!

21:59.920 --> 22:02.790
My demonic power is this indomitable body!

22:02.920 --> 22:04.420
Naotsugu! Run away!

22:05.750 --> 22:06.790
Naotsugu!

22:09.960 --> 22:11.580
Jin-dono...

22:16.540 --> 22:17.920
Just get out of here already!

22:17.920 --> 22:18.830
I'm sorry!

22:27.420 --> 22:28.630
What are you doing?!

22:29.540 --> 22:31.880
My target is Naotsugu Miura.

22:32.250 --> 22:34.880
There's no point in fighting now that he's gone.

22:35.920 --> 22:37.710
Remember what I told you before?

22:38.460 --> 22:40.790
Demons are incompatible with humans.

22:41.290 --> 22:43.830
Well? Those words ring quite true now, don't they?

22:54.630 --> 22:56.210
L-look at that freak!

22:56.500 --> 22:58.080
Hey, I know him!

23:01.960 --> 23:03.210
Daddy...

23:20.670 --> 23:21.670
Daddy?!
